1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:01,910
The year is AD 110.

2
00:00:03,770 --> 00:00:07,590
You are standing on a street
in Rome, capital of an empire

3
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:09,590
stretching across the Mediterranean.

4
00:00:10,890 --> 00:00:13,730
Beyond the rooftops stands the Colosseum.

5
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:16,610
Aqueducts carry water for miles.

6
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:21,430
Temples, markets, workshops,
and crowded apartment blocks

7
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:25,130
fill the city. And you have a problem.

8
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:28,030
You have no money anyone recognizes.

9
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:33,270
No home, no family, nobody to vouch

10
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:37,750
for you. Even if you studied
Latin, the voices around

11
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:41,290
you move quickly and many
people speak other languages.

12
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:45,850
At first, Rome looks strangely familiar.

13
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:51,350
There are bakeries,
traffic, rented rooms, and

14
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:53,050
food sold across counters.

15
00:00:53,810 --> 00:00:56,990
But none of the systems
you rely on exists here.

16
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:01,570
No telephone, no modern hospital,

17
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:07,030
no card payment, no official identification

18
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:08,810
that makes sense to anyone.

19
00:01:09,730 --> 00:01:12,630
You know more about the
future than anyone alive.

20
00:01:14,270 --> 00:01:17,450
Yet that knowledge will not
buy you a loaf of bread.

21
00:01:18,510 --> 00:01:20,390
Your first challenge is simple.

22
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:23,050
Survive until nightfall.

23
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:27,860
The heat rises from the paving stones.

24
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:32,840
Smoke from ovens mixes with
animal smells and the noise of

25
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:37,170
carts. Before you can work out

26
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:39,830
where you are going, you need water.

27
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:45,560
Rome's aqueducts are an
engineering triumph.

28
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:50,440
Gravity carries water from
distant sources into the city.

29
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:54,280
Public fountains put some of
it within reach of ordinary

30
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:58,120
residents. You may be able
to drink without paying.

31
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:02,650
But this is not a

32
00:02:02,650 --> 00:02:07,190
modern treatment network. Roman
engineers understand water

33
00:02:07,190 --> 00:02:11,630
flow, not bacteria. Sewage and

34
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:15,610
waste exist alongside the city's
impressive infrastructure.

35
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:21,530
Water quality varies, and a
fountain is not a guarantee

36
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:25,650
against illness. Then comes hunger.

37
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:31,290
Bread, olives, cheese, fruit and cooked

38
00:02:31,290 --> 00:02:34,030
food are available in
markets and street shops.

39
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:39,530
You recognize the ingredients,
but you cannot recognize the

40
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:42,990
prices. Your bank notes mean nothing.

41
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:48,550
Your phone has no network, and
your bank balance might as well

42
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:49,690
be on another planet.

43
00:02:50,490 --> 00:02:55,730
Food is everywhere. Food you can
actually obtain is another matter.

44
00:02:58,412 --> 00:03:02,312
As daylight fades, you notice
the buildings above you.

45
00:03:03,092 --> 00:03:06,292
Wealthy households live
behind courtyard entrances.

46
00:03:07,592 --> 00:03:12,072
Many others rent rooms in
multi-story blocks, where space can

47
00:03:12,072 --> 00:03:15,992
be cramped, and cooking fires
and oil lamps create risks.

48
00:03:17,252 --> 00:03:20,132
Rome has experienced catastrophic fires.

49
00:03:21,172 --> 00:03:25,452
After the great fire of
AD-64, the authorities

50
00:03:25,452 --> 00:03:29,592
introduced precautions, but
crowded buildings remain

51
00:03:29,592 --> 00:03:33,872
vulnerable. The streets sound

52
00:03:33,872 --> 00:03:36,832
different after dark. Shops close.

53
00:03:38,032 --> 00:03:42,552
People retreat indoors. Wagons, restricted

54
00:03:42,552 --> 00:03:46,992
in some busy daytime
streets, rumble through the

55
00:03:46,992 --> 00:03:51,572
night. You hear wheels, animals, and

56
00:03:51,572 --> 00:03:53,632
voices echoing between walls.

57
00:03:54,352 --> 00:03:57,872
You could look for a cheap
room, if someone will accept you

58
00:03:57,872 --> 00:04:01,972
without money. You could
try a sheltered doorway.

59
00:04:03,872 --> 00:04:06,432
Neither offers the security of a home.

60
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:12,352
And being exhausted in an unfamiliar
city makes every decision

61
00:04:12,352 --> 00:04:16,602
harder. Less than a day has passed.

62
00:04:18,002 --> 00:04:20,922
You are learning something
no monument can teach.

63
00:04:22,142 --> 00:04:25,202
Surviving here depends
on people who know you.

64
00:04:25,202 --> 00:04:27,762
And you know nobody.

65
00:04:30,384 --> 00:04:34,584
The Rome of Marble Statues is
also a city of exhausting work.

66
00:04:35,604 --> 00:04:39,344
Bakers rise early. Porters unload sacks.

67
00:04:40,284 --> 00:04:44,504
Builders, traders, artisans,
cleaners, and sailors

68
00:04:44,504 --> 00:04:46,044
keep the capital running.

69
00:04:47,204 --> 00:04:51,684
Some workers are free, others
are enslaved, and labor

70
00:04:51,684 --> 00:04:53,924
without freedom to choose their lives.

71
00:04:55,164 --> 00:04:57,144
You approach someone unloading goods.

72
00:04:57,864 --> 00:05:01,504
Perhaps you could carry baskets
or sweep a shop in exchange

73
00:05:01,504 --> 00:05:04,324
for bread. You have the strength.

74
00:05:05,464 --> 00:05:08,544
But why should a stranger
trust you with their stock?

75
00:05:09,384 --> 00:05:10,724
Who can recommend you?

76
00:05:11,364 --> 00:05:13,124
What happens if something goes missing?

77
00:05:14,364 --> 00:05:17,184
You might find an employer
willing to take a chance.

78
00:05:18,144 --> 00:05:20,644
You might not. You might not.

79
00:05:21,424 --> 00:05:25,724
You might not. The city's
grain distributions are

80
00:05:25,724 --> 00:05:28,684
not a universal emergency food service.

81
00:05:29,384 --> 00:05:33,064
Access depends on eligibility and status.

82
00:05:34,064 --> 00:05:38,584
Even receiving grain does
not mean someone cooks it for

83
00:05:38,584 --> 00:05:42,784
you. For an ordinary
Roman, local relationships

84
00:05:42,784 --> 00:05:44,844
can turn effort into a living.

85
00:05:44,844 --> 00:05:49,384
For you, the absence of
those relationships can

86
00:05:49,384 --> 00:05:52,084
turn one missed meal into another.

87
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:57,870
And by the third day, the
city begins to make sense.

88
00:05:59,070 --> 00:06:03,210
You recognize a fountain. You
follow the smell of fresh bread.

89
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:05,750
Then you enter a public bath.

90
00:06:06,790 --> 00:06:09,990
There are changing areas,
heated rooms, and pools.

91
00:06:11,190 --> 00:06:14,310
Beneath some floors, hot
air circulates through brick

92
00:06:14,310 --> 00:06:18,550
supports. Baths are places
for washing, exercise,

93
00:06:19,730 --> 00:06:23,210
conversation, and business. Some
are affordable for ordinary

94
00:06:23,210 --> 00:06:26,670
residents. This is not a primitive society.

95
00:06:27,750 --> 00:06:30,350
But impressive engineering is
not the same as modern health

96
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:34,610
care. Shared surfaces, waste
channels, and crowded facilities

97
00:06:34,610 --> 00:06:37,250
exist without an understanding of microbes.

98
00:06:38,450 --> 00:06:42,410
Roman sanitation is real, but
so are parasites and infection.

99
00:06:43,750 --> 00:06:45,850
Doctors have practical
knowledge and instruments.

100
00:06:46,770 --> 00:06:48,770
They can dress wounds and
treat some conditions.

101
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:51,010
Yet they have no antibiotics.

102
00:06:51,010 --> 00:06:55,370
A small injury that becomes
infected can threaten your

103
00:06:55,370 --> 00:06:58,250
ability to work, and
therefore your ability to eat.

104
00:06:59,350 --> 00:07:01,310
The bathhouse reveals Rome's contradiction.

105
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:05,850
Extraordinary public technology
alongside vulnerabilities that

106
00:07:05,850 --> 00:07:07,550
modern life makes easy to forget.

107
00:07:09,742 --> 00:07:13,322
On the fourth day, you notice
a different kind of danger,

108
00:07:13,862 --> 00:07:17,622
status. Rome is full of citizens,

109
00:07:18,302 --> 00:07:22,442
freed people, migrants,
visitors, and enslaved people.

110
00:07:23,002 --> 00:07:27,102
Wealth, sex, family
connections, and legal position

111
00:07:27,102 --> 00:07:31,282
shape what someone can own,
where they can work, and how

112
00:07:31,282 --> 00:07:35,762
disputes are handled. Latin
is common, but you may

113
00:07:35,762 --> 00:07:39,322
also hear Greek and other
languages from across the empire.

114
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:43,682
You cannot simply assume everyone
is equal before the law,

115
00:07:44,182 --> 00:07:48,302
nor does being an unknown
stranger mean someone can

116
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:52,742
automatically enslave you.
The rules are more complicated

117
00:07:52,742 --> 00:07:56,682
than either story. A patron, household,

118
00:07:57,242 --> 00:08:01,122
or employer could give you an
introduction and a place in the

119
00:08:01,122 --> 00:08:05,362
city's social networks.
Without one, even explaining

120
00:08:05,362 --> 00:08:07,322
who you are becomes difficult.

121
00:08:08,902 --> 00:08:11,902
You came from a world where
identity can be checked in

122
00:08:11,902 --> 00:08:16,322
seconds. Here, a trusted
person's word may matter

123
00:08:16,322 --> 00:08:18,762
more than anything you
can say about yourself.

124
00:08:21,069 --> 00:08:24,829
You wake with a headache,
maybe it is heat, hunger, or

125
00:08:24,829 --> 00:08:28,449
exhaustion. Maybe the food
or water disagreed with you.

126
00:08:29,129 --> 00:08:33,429
You cannot know. Rome has
physicians and medical

127
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:36,309
traditions shaped by
Greek and Roman learning.

128
00:08:37,529 --> 00:08:41,309
Some treatments help. But
without modern diagnostics,

129
00:08:41,629 --> 00:08:45,769
antibiotics, or reliable
rehydration treatment, an infection

130
00:08:45,769 --> 00:08:49,189
or severe stomach illness can
become much more dangerous.

131
00:08:50,009 --> 00:08:53,249
Do not misunderstand
ancient life expectancy.

132
00:08:55,729 --> 00:08:59,789
High infant and childhood
mortality lowered the average.

133
00:09:01,209 --> 00:09:04,229
It does not mean that every
Roman adult died young.

134
00:09:05,349 --> 00:09:06,909
Many survived for decades.

135
00:09:08,769 --> 00:09:11,269
And you might survive this illness too.

136
00:09:12,469 --> 00:09:15,609
But a swollen foot can
stop you carrying loads.

137
00:09:16,529 --> 00:09:20,289
Missing work can mean missing food.

138
00:09:21,229 --> 00:09:25,309
Severe dehydration can make
the walk to a fountain feel

139
00:09:25,309 --> 00:09:29,769
impossible. The threat is

140
00:09:29,769 --> 00:09:33,469
not necessarily a gladiator,
an emperor, or a soldier.

141
00:09:34,189 --> 00:09:38,749
Sometimes it is a small
medical problem arriving when

142
00:09:38,749 --> 00:09:42,489
you have no money, no
shelter, and nobody to help.

143
00:09:48,776 --> 00:09:51,436
You stand near a monumental
public building.

144
00:09:52,336 --> 00:09:53,856
The crowd moves around you.

145
00:09:54,596 --> 00:09:58,136
People arguing, selling,
delivering, and hurrying to work.

146
00:09:59,196 --> 00:10:02,696
This is the Rome remembered in
films, but it survives because

147
00:10:02,696 --> 00:10:04,856
of people who rarely appear in those films.

148
00:10:06,036 --> 00:10:07,616
Grain arrives by ship and cart.

149
00:10:08,496 --> 00:10:11,696
Bakers know suppliers.
Porters know employers.

150
00:10:12,556 --> 00:10:15,936
Traders know customers.
Neighbors know which rooms are

151
00:10:15,936 --> 00:10:20,216
available. Families and
communities share knowledge, labor,

152
00:10:20,456 --> 00:10:24,596
and support. These connections
do not erase poverty or

153
00:10:24,596 --> 00:10:28,196
exploitation. Some residents
have comfortable lives.

154
00:10:29,496 --> 00:10:31,936
Others survive with almost
no margin for bad luck.

155
00:10:32,896 --> 00:10:37,096
But the difference between you
and an ordinary worker is not

156
00:10:37,096 --> 00:10:39,336
simply physical strength or intelligence.

157
00:10:40,276 --> 00:10:44,636
They know how this city works,
because they belong to it.

158
00:10:46,016 --> 00:10:48,496
You brought modern knowledge with you.

159
00:10:49,096 --> 00:10:52,276
You did not bring the relationships
that turn knowledge into

160
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:55,236
food, shelter, and a livelihood.

161
00:10:59,585 --> 00:11:01,245
A week has passed.

162
00:11:02,605 --> 00:11:05,465
The morning sun touches Rome's rooftops.

163
00:11:06,245 --> 00:11:07,985
Water runs into a fountain.

164
00:11:08,945 --> 00:11:10,345
A baker opens a shop.

165
00:11:11,345 --> 00:11:12,845
A family prepares breakfast.

166
00:11:14,485 --> 00:11:15,665
The city carries on.

167
00:11:17,605 --> 00:11:19,525
And perhaps you are still alive.

168
00:11:21,245 --> 00:11:25,465
That matters. It would
be wrong to claim that

169
00:11:25,465 --> 00:11:29,425
every modern visitor must
die within seven days.

170
00:11:31,005 --> 00:11:35,105
A healthy person who finds
clean enough water, food,

171
00:11:35,765 --> 00:11:39,565
shelter, and help could
survive much longer.

172
00:11:40,345 --> 00:11:42,605
But your smartphone is useless.

173
00:11:44,165 --> 00:11:46,005
Your savings do not exist here.

174
00:11:46,765 --> 00:11:49,005
Modern medicine cannot follow you.

175
00:11:49,005 --> 00:11:53,125
You cannot assume that somebody
will recognize your identity

176
00:11:53,125 --> 00:11:55,205
or offer emergency assistance.

177
00:11:56,345 --> 00:11:59,745
The Romans were not foolish
people waiting to be rescued by

178
00:11:59,745 --> 00:12:04,125
the future. They built an
extraordinary city and they

179
00:12:04,125 --> 00:12:05,705
learned to live within it.

180
00:12:06,765 --> 00:12:10,445
You are the one without the
skills, trusted contacts,

181
00:12:11,645 --> 00:12:13,685
or recognized place in society.

182
00:12:14,425 --> 00:12:17,905
If you survive the week, it
may not be because you were

183
00:12:17,905 --> 00:12:19,065
stronger than the Romans.

184
00:12:20,705 --> 00:12:24,345
It may be because someone
showed you how to belong.

185
00:12:25,425 --> 00:12:29,585
So if you woke up in Rome
tomorrow, who would help you?

